What is not in this repository
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The TCP core - the transport that carries a live database session from one host
to another - is developed separately and is NOT part of this Apache-licensed
distribution. It is not covered by the LICENSE file and no rights to it are
granted here. Enquiries: https://seclume.space/

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party code
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

None. seclume implements the PostgreSQL, MySQL, TDS and Oracle TTC wire
protocols itself and depends on nothing outside the JDK at runtime. The Spring
Boot starter depends on Spring, which the application brings anyway.

Test and build tooling (JUnit, Spring Boot, Flyway, Maven plugins) is declared
in the POMs and carries its own licences; none of it is redistributed here.
